# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
# virtual environments, wherever a README's `python -m venv` / `uv sync` puts them (fix wave 25, scout C5-8)
.venv/
venv/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Secrets: every service refuses to start without bearer tokens, and the READMEs tell you to export them; a local
# .env holding them must never be committed (gitleaks does not recognise arbitrary shared-secret strings).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Go (`go build ./cmd/orchestrator` writes `orchestrator`; `go build` at the module root writes `orchestrator-go`)
/services/orchestrator-go/orchestrator-go
/services/orchestrator-go/orchestrator
*.test
coverage.out

# Rust
target/
# Cargo.lock is intentionally tracked (not ignored): ledger-rust ships a
# binary (server), and binaries should commit their lockfile for
# reproducible builds.

# Ledger and department runtime logs — generated at runtime, per environment, never committed (evidence data, not
# source). Fix wave 26b (scout C5-8b): scoped to the names the services write — ledger-rust's default
# ledger_data/ledger.jsonl, the departments' <dept>_log.jsonl in their data dirs, and the `.torn-*` side files the
# torn-tail recovery writes next to a log — instead of `*.jsonl` repo-wide, which made a JSONL test fixture anywhere
# but ledger-rust's tests/fixtures silently un-addable.
ledger_data/
ledger.jsonl
cn_log.jsonl
compliance_log.jsonl
dlv_log.jsonl
fin_log.jsonl
legal_log.jsonl
vi_log.jsonl
*.jsonl.torn-*

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
next-env.d.ts
npm-debug.log*
coverage/

# OS
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
